1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:21,987
Professor: O 'bii' — am, is, are — você já tem no presente. Mas e no PASSADO? São só duas caras: 'am' e 'is' (I, he, she, it) viram 'was'; 'are' (you, we, they) vira 'were'. E tanto faz 'era', de ser, ou 'estava', de estar — os dois viram 'was'. Escuta — 'eu estava aqui':

2
00:00:22,487 --> 00:00:23,462
Professor: I was here.

3
00:00:24,688 --> 00:00:25,710
Bia: I was here.

4
00:00:27,686 --> 00:00:29,033
Professor: 'ele estava cansado':

5
00:00:32,105 --> 00:00:33,545
Bia: He was tired.

6
00:00:35,348 --> 00:00:39,249
Professor: Agora o 'were', pra you, we, they: 'você estava feliz':

7
00:00:39,749 --> 00:00:40,771
Professor: You were happy.

8
00:00:41,857 --> 00:00:43,204
Bia: You were happy.

9
00:00:44,965 --> 00:00:49,470
Professor: 'eles estavam lá' — e ó, 'lá' de lugar é 'there'. 'eles estavam lá':

10
00:00:52,507 --> 00:00:53,714
Bia: They were there.

11
00:00:55,364 --> 00:00:57,732
Professor: E a do dia, com esse 'there': 'eu estava lá':

12
00:01:00,801 --> 00:01:01,962
Bia: I was there.

13
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:09,660
Bia: Ah — então é só o 'bii' no passado? 'was' pro eu, ele, ela; 'were' pro você, nós, eles?

14
00:01:11,296 --> 00:01:22,024
Professor: Exato — 'was' pro UM só (I, he, she, it), 'were' pro resto. E como é o be, nega e pergunta igualzinho. Sente agora contra antes — 'eu tava feliz':

15
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:27,011
Bia: I was happy.

16
00:01:28,196 --> 00:01:29,357
Professor: 'ela tava cansada':

17
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:33,787
Bia: She was tired.

18
00:01:35,728 --> 00:01:48,963
Professor: Nega com 'not' — e lembra: 'isn't' é 'is' e 'not' colados. No passado, mesma cola: 'was' e 'not' vira 'wasn't', 'were' e 'not' vira 'weren't'. Escuta:

19
00:01:49,463 --> 00:01:51,553
Professor: I wasn't there. They weren't here.

20
00:01:52,053 --> 00:01:54,886
Professor: Agora você: 'ela não tava aqui':

21
00:01:58,282 --> 00:01:59,629
Bia: She wasn't here.

22
00:02:02,093 --> 00:02:03,208
Professor: e 'eles não tavam lá':

23
00:02:06,254 --> 00:02:07,554
Bia: They weren't there.

24
00:02:09,841 --> 00:02:14,485
Professor: E pra perguntar, você vira o be na frente sozinho. 'você tava lá?' — manda:

25
00:02:17,774 --> 00:02:18,796
Bia: Were you there?

26
00:02:20,012 --> 00:02:24,192
Professor: Isso, o be pergunta sozinho. Responde curto: 'tava? — sim':

27
00:02:27,309 --> 00:02:28,656
Bia: Yes, I was.

28
00:02:30,118 --> 00:02:31,186
Professor: 'a gente tava lá':

29
00:02:35,002 --> 00:02:36,163
Bia: We was there.

30
00:02:36,663 --> 00:02:39,171
Bia: ...peraí, 'we' pede 'were', não 'was', né?

31
00:02:41,043 --> 00:02:43,969
Professor: Cravou — 'we were there'. De novo:

32
00:02:47,607 --> 00:02:48,814
Bia: We were there.

33
00:02:50,372 --> 00:02:52,276
Professor: 'ele tava aqui, e eles tavam lá':

34
00:02:55,823 --> 00:02:58,052
Bia: He was here, and they were there.

35
00:02:59,146 --> 00:03:02,304
Professor: Recombina com um cognato: 'o problema era importante':

36
00:03:03,393 --> 00:03:11,009
Bia: Hmm... 'problema' eu tenho, é 'problem'... e 'importante' é cognato, quase idêntico. Acho que sei:

37
00:03:11,509 --> 00:03:13,552
Bia: The problem was important.

38
00:03:15,572 --> 00:03:22,492
Professor: Isso! 'importante' vira 'important', e 'era' é 'was' — viu? ser ou estar, no inglês é o mesmo 'was'.

39
00:03:22,992 --> 00:03:26,661
Professor: E traz o 'dar' de volta: 'eu posso te dar o carro, mas eu não tava lá':

40
00:03:29,975 --> 00:03:32,808
Bia: I can give you the car, but I wasn't there.

41
00:03:34,686 --> 00:03:36,869
Professor: 'eu não trabalho aqui, mas eu tava aqui hoje':

42
00:03:40,322 --> 00:03:43,016
Bia: I don't work here, but I was here today.

43
00:03:44,465 --> 00:03:46,741
Professor: 'ela tava cansada, então ela não pode te ajudar':

44
00:03:50,535 --> 00:03:53,600
Bia: She was tired, so she can't help you.

45
00:03:55,648 --> 00:04:01,017
Professor: E aquele 'there' de 'there is' — 'tem' — no passado vira 'there were'. 'tinha três carros':

46
00:04:04,261 --> 00:04:06,026
Bia: There were three cars.

47
00:04:07,887 --> 00:04:11,091
Professor: E fecha, antes contra agora: 'eu tava lá, mas eu tô aqui agora':

48
00:04:14,616 --> 00:04:16,706
Bia: I was there, but I am here now.

49
00:04:19,018 --> 00:04:34,715
Professor: Sacou? 'was' e 'were' é o be no passado — 'was' pro um, 'were' pro resto. Nega com 'not', pergunta virando, responde com ele. E ó: verbo de AÇÃO, tipo trabalhar e falar, tem OUTRO passado — o 'ed' — que vem já já.

50
00:04:36,809 --> 00:04:43,311
Bia: Boa — 'I was there'. O passado do be é só a outra cara dele. Agora eu falo do que já foi!

